# Shared by two build contexts rooted at backend/: the Node API image
# (backend/Dockerfile) and the AI interviewer image
# (backend/AI_interviewer/Dockerfile, which needs Mentor_Mentee_Match as a
# sibling and so must build from here). Keep exclusions valid for both.

# 258 MB of Windows-native binaries (mongod.exe, *-win32-x64-msvc) that are
# useless in a Linux image and would poison npm ci layer caching.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Secrets are injected at runtime (SSM -> ECS task definition), never baked.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Python build/test artifacts. **/venv (not */venv) because Rag_Chatbot's is
# two levels deep (Rag_Chatbot/app/venv) — a single */venv only matches one
# path segment and silently let a multi-GB torch venv into the build context
# (582MB -> 2.05GB on the Node image, caught via `docker history`).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coveragerc
htmlcov/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

# Tests never run inside the runtime image
test/
tests/
conftest.py
**/conftest.py
pytest.ini
reports/
test-results/
coverage/

# Stale file-based session store, superseded by MongoDB
AI_interviewer/sessions/

# Referenced by zero code (no migrate_faqs_to_mongo.py exists in this repo)
Rag_Chatbot/faqs_seed.json

# Ephemeral in ECS anyway — CV uploads need S3/Cloudinary to survive a deploy
uploads/

# One-off maintenance/seed scripts, not part of the serving path
scripts/

.git/
.gitignore
*.md
